From: Jack Ma <jack4it@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Backport VXLAN FDB nexthop UDP destination ports to 6.6

Allow VXLAN FDB nexthops sharing an underlay IP to select different UDP
destination ports. Nexthops without an explicit port retain the device default.

Upstream series:
https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260724-b4-vxlan-fdb-port-v5-0-cd1c6aeee058@gmail.com/

Upstream: 53531e6a644a48c2d5a9423f084ae4e91ec6019a
Upstream: 951085f82873dc53a62181499a7a7f77b70f9343
Upstream: 992965451db727a15988931655a825c5e0312edb
Upstream: 2c9fb925c2ccc6ee475134840cff6c6b73851730

The 6.6 adaptation reserves upstream attribute IDs 14-17 to keep NHA_DST_PORT
at 18, accepts zero-valued operation flags on legacy GET requests, and uses
TC counters for the selftests without backporting nexthop statistics.
Includes IPv4/IPv6 destination-port, ECMP, fallback, learning and proxy coverage.

Original feature author: Jack Ma <jack4it@gmail.com>
Original VXLAN selftest foundation author: Ido Schimmel <idosch@nvidia.com>
Original feature backport: Hamza Mahfooz <hamzamahfooz@linux.microsoft.com>

